# Backend Rules

Use Python type hints throughout.

Use Pydantic at external boundaries.

Keep FastAPI routes thin.

Routes should:

1. validate request
2. call service
3. return response

Business logic belongs in services.

Analytics functions should preferably be pure deterministic functions.

Scoring functions must not call the LLM.

Data providers should normalize external APIs into internal Pydantic models.

External API formats must not leak into analytics or scoring.

Use async HTTP calls with httpx where appropriate.

All external requests must have timeouts.

Do not expose secrets or raw internal exceptions.

Use explicit exceptions from core/exceptions.py.

Missing numerical data must remain None or explicitly unavailable.

Never silently convert missing values to zero.

Scores must be clamped to their documented range.

Keep scoring weights centralized.

Tests should directly cover deterministic calculations.

Prefer dependency injection through function/class arguments over complex frameworks.

Before adding a new backend module, check docs/CODEBASE_MAP.md to determine whether an existing module already owns that responsibility.